 "faq_text": "What Should I Wear to a Thai Massage? You stay fully clothed, so wear something loose and comfortable that lets you move easily. What Will I Lie On? Thai massage is done on a mat. I guide each movement and check in with you as I go. How Long Is a Session? Sessions are 60 or 90 minutes. If you are not sure which to choose, tell me what you would like from the session and I will help you decide. Do I Need to Be Flexible? No. I set the range of each stretch by what is comfortable for you, and I never force one. You can ask me to change or skip any movement. Where Do Sessions Take Place? Sessions take place in Mt. Tabor, Portland. I do not currently travel to clients. How Is Thai Massage Different From Your Other Services? Thai massage is done fully clothed on a mat and combines steady pressure and gentle rocking with assisted stretching. Therapeutic Massage and Deep Tissue Massage are described on their own pages. How Do I Book a Session? Use the Contact page to reach me by phone or email, and tell me what you would like. I will reply to arrange a time."
